  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile with scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer/concat (config_012, acc=0.721) and avgpool/concat (config_049, acc=0.715) are the current best, both far above singleprofile (0.532). The RNA encoder dimension is completely unexplored—we've only tested scvi_n200. This experiment tests scgpt (a generative pre-trained RNA encoder) while holding all other proven-optimal components fixed (multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, concat fusion). This is the highest-information-gain next step: if scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the right encoder and we can focus remaining budget on fusion and image-encoder variations. With 6 experiments still remaining after this, the risk of a negative result is manageable. Expected cost: comparable to config_012 (~4.5–5 GPU hours), as the dominant costs (ViT-L image processing, transformer aggregation over multiple profiles) are unchanged; scgpt's per-sample encoding cost is similar in magnitude to scvi_n200."
